# Task scope tags (mandatory)

Default is `[fullstack]` when no tag is given. The tag affects **layer coverage only** — every other rule file stays mandatory regardless of tag.

| Tag | Touch |
|-----|-------|
| `[fullstack]` | API + SPA (sibling repo) + translations + menu route registry parity + user-facing page |
| `[backend]` | API layer only: routes, controllers, form requests, policies, repositories, resources, migrations, models, tests |
| `[frontend]` | SPA layer in `monolith-vue-workers` only (assumes the API already exists) |
| `[docs]` | User-facing page in the sibling `docs` site (Docusaurus) — the customer's manual, no code layer |

## `[fullstack]` layer table

| Layer | What to touch |
|-------|----------------|
| API | Versioned routes `/api/v1/*`, controllers, form requests, policies, repositories, resources |
| Web (server) | `routes/web/*.php` only — public share, payment return, OAuth callback. No Blade views |
| SPA | Screens, forms, listings in `monolith-vue-workers` |
| Docs (user-facing) | The page in the sibling `docs` site that teaches the capability — a customer-visible change without it is incomplete (that repo's `docs-sync.mdc`) |
| Navigation | Menu `route` column = SPA Vue Router symbolic name; keep `config/spa-routes.php` ↔ `MenuSeeder` ↔ SPA router in sync |
| Translation | All user-facing strings, every supported locale |
| API shape | Canonical envelope only — see `api-resources.mdc` |
| Other | Migrations, seeders, models, events/listeners, notifications, tests, the owning brief + rule file |

An API-only or SPA-only change without its counterpart layers is **incomplete** unless the tag says otherwise.
